# TFP_VALUES_LIST

Inventory of **values and artifacts** the TFP (Transference-Focused Psychotherapy–oriented) stack can emit in this repository: what each bundle contains, where operators consume it, prerequisites, and calibration touchpoints.  
Canonical wiring: `runtime/pipeline/run_tfp_file_pipeline.py`, `tools/gena_tfp_bundle_run.py`, `docs/governance/working/ETHAN-TFP-RUNNABLE-DICT-WIRING.md`, `docs/specs/TFP_CALIBRATION_KNOBS_v0_1.md`.

**Scope note:** TFP bundles are **research / testing grounds**, not the sealed v0.5.1 public product proof (`00_manifest.json` → `scope_note`).

---

## 0. One bundle directory — not multiple “canons”

**Rule:** For a given run, **exactly one directory** (`--out-dir`) holds the **whole** file-pipeline artifact set (`00`–`09`, optional `12_*`, sidecars). That directory is the **only** place to look for that run’s outputs. Do not assume two different tools wrote to the same path unless you passed the **same** `--out-dir` / `-o`.

**Why chats get wasted:** Different CLIs use **different default output roots**. None of them is “more canonical” than another — they are different wrappers. If you compare runs across sessions without noting **which tool** and **which out path**, you will open the wrong folder.

| Entrypoint | Default output directory (if you omit `-o` / `--out-dir`) |
|------------|---------------------------------------------------------------|
| `python3 tools/gena_tfp_bundle_run.py -i <file>` | `<repo>/outputs/tfp/runs/tfp_gena_<input_stem>/` |
| `python3 tools/tfp_pipeline_standard_run.py -i <file>` | `<repo>/outputs/tfp/runs/tfp_pipeline_run/<uuid>/` (new UUID each run) |
| `python3 -m runtime.pipeline.run_tfp_file_pipeline …` | `<repo>/outputs/tfp/runs/tfp_pipeline_run/<run_id>/` |

**On-disk layout under `outputs/` (see `outputs/README.md`):** TFP-named runs and smoke dirs live under **`outputs/tfp/`** — `tfp/runs/` (bundles, calibration passes, session experiments), `tfp/smoke/` (wiring / triz smoke), `tfp/tool/` (e.g. API one-shot). Symlinks at `outputs/latest_tfp_calibration_run` and `outputs/prev_tfp_calibration_run` point into `tfp/runs/`. Other top-level dirs (`benchmarks/`, `dict_calibration/`, `e2e/`, `reports/`, …) stay for non–file-pipeline harnesses.

**Operator narrative fixture (tracked):** `tests/fixtures/tfp/input.txt` — long-form Russian clinical-style session text for TFP runs; do not relocate or overwrite without updating this line and any tooling that references it.

**Recommended operator habit:** Use defaults under `outputs/tfp/runs/` or set **explicit** `-o` (e.g. `outputs/tfp/runs/my_experiment`) when you need a stable name. Standardize on **one** wrapper (`gena_tfp_bundle_run.py` for audit + schema + optional gold + gate) when comparing runs.

**Input text (TFP file pipeline):** The engine sees **the file you pass** to `-i` / `--input` (plain text, `.md`, or `sessions[]` JSON). Pipeline forces `HESPERIA_DLCR_DOMAIN_PACK=tfp` unless `--no-dlcr-domain-pack` (see `00_manifest.json` → `flags`). There is no parallel “default sphere sentence” path for this CLI — your **input file is the session**.

**What is not automatically in that same folder:**

- **`10_` / `11_`** — Produced when you run **`gena_tfp_bundle_run`** post-steps (audit + gate), not by raw `run_tfp_file_pipeline` alone.
- **`99_tfp_bundle_inspect.json`** — From **`tfp_pipeline_standard_run.py`** when `--inspect`, or inspection tooling on an existing bundle.
- **API / one-shot sidecars** (`tfp_api_calibration_one_shot`, etc.) — Separate tool; separate `-o` directory unless you copy files yourself.
- **E2E harness JSON** under repo `assets/artifacts/e2e/` (or similar) — **Different runners** (`run_e2e_all` and friends), not the file pipeline. Treat as **another product** unless a future consolidation tool copies or regenerates into your bundle (not part of baseline `run_tfp_file_pipeline` in this tree).

**Consolidated “full dossier” artifacts** (e.g. `20_main_engine_full_context.json`, `21_hesperia_environment_snapshot.json`, optional `CONSOLIDATION_MANIFEST.json`, generated `e2e_snapshot/`) — when present in a bundle, they come from **additional** tools/commits layered on the file pipeline; they are **not** implied by `run_tfp_file_pipeline` alone. Check the Hesperia branch/tool that added them before assuming they exist in every checkout.

